# COPY REGENT OF PROBOLINGGO

# EAST JAVA PROVINCE

# REGIONAL REGULATION OF PROBOLINGGO REGENCY

# NUMBER: 2 OF 2019

# CONCERNING

# IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN

# BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

# REGENT OF PROBOLINGGO,

Considering:  
a. that women and children are creatures of God Almighty who have human rights guaranteed by the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia, therefore women and children must be protected from all forms of violence and discrimination;  
b. that violence against women and children in the Region tends to increase, therefore the Regional Government and/or community need to play an active role optimally to provide protection, so that women and children are prevented and free from violence or threats of violence, torture, or treatment that degrades human dignity and honor;  
c. that protection of women and children is a mandatory concurrent affair which is the authority, obligation, and responsibility of the Regional Government, therefore regulation is needed as a basis for implementing comprehensive and integrated protection for women and children;  
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Implementation of Protection for Women and Children.  

In View of:  
1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;  

2. Law Number 12 of 1950 concerning Formation of Regency Regions within the Province of East Java (State Gazette of 1950 Number 41) as amended by Law Number 2 of 1965 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1965 Number 19, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 2730);  
3. Law Number 4 of 1979 concerning Child Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1979 Number 32, Supplement to State Gazette Number 3143);  
4. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on The Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia 3668);  
5. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);  
6. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3143) as last amended by Law Number 17 of 2016 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2016 Number 237, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5946);  
7. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);  
8. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 64, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635);  
9. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);  
10. Law Number 12 of 2011 concerning Formation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 82, Supplement to State Gazette 5234);  
11. Law Number 11 of 2012 concerning Juvenile Justice System (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2012 Number 153 Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5332);  
12. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5512) as amended several times most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 24, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5657);  
13. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia number 64);  
14. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2008 concerning Implementation of Women's Protection;  
15. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 3 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for Implementation of Child Protection;  
16. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 5 of 2010 concerning Guidelines for Establishment and Development of Integrated Service Centers (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2010 Number 446);  
17. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 2 of 2011 concerning Empowerment of Child Victims of Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 42);  
18. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 19 of 2011 concerning Empowerment of Women Victims of Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 903);  
19. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 6 of 2015 concerning System for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 903);  
20. Regional Regulation of East Java Province Number 16 of 2012 concerning Implementation of Protection for Women and Child Victims of Violence (Regional Gazette of East Java Province of 2013 Number 3 Series D, Supplement to Regional Gazette of East Java Province Number 23);  
21. Regional Regulation of East Java Province Number 2 of 2014 concerning Implementation of Child Protection (Regional Gazette of East Java Province of 2014 Number 2 Series D, Supplement to Regional Gazette of East Java Province Number 38);  
22. Regional Regulation of Probolinggo Regency Number 6 of 2016 concerning Formation and Composition of Regional Apparatus.  

With Mutual Approval of THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF PROBOLINGGO REGENCY and

# REGENT OF PROBOLINGGO

# HAS DECIDED:

To Establish: REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN.

